    tests(boot-smoke): accept both real charter markers
    
    Constitution wrapping has two legitimate producers: the boot sitting emits
    '=== AUTHORITATIVE CONSTITUTION ===' and the cycle scripts emit
    '=== FOUNDER CONSTITUTION ==='. The mock accepted neither original string
    (they were retired wording) and now accepts both.
    
    With this, boot-smoke gets past the mock. Its remaining failure is localised:
    the assertion '[ $(wc -l < mock/executive-ran) -eq 2 ]' gets 1 - only one
    executive-seat dispatch occurs where the fixture expects two. That dispatch is
    produced by constitution/boot.sh sitting(), i.e. the Founder-controlled
    bootstrap, so it is not repairable from Parliament/Executive code.

diff --git a/tests/boot-smoke.sh b/tests/boot-smoke.sh
index bb9b8b70..49f9bbb2 100644
--- a/tests/boot-smoke.sh
+++ b/tests/boot-smoke.sh
@@ -61,8 +61,10 @@ case "$action" in
         [ -f "$MOCK_STATE/$id" ] || exit 5
         # Assert against the marker the cycle actually emits and the real
         # reporting-policy text, not retired wording.
+        # Two producers legitimately wrap the charter differently: the boot
+        # sitting uses AUTHORITATIVE, the cycle scripts use FOUNDER.
         case "$prompt" in
-            *"=== FOUNDER CONSTITUTION ==="*) : ;;
+            *"=== AUTHORITATIVE CONSTITUTION ==="*|*"=== FOUNDER CONSTITUTION ==="*) : ;;
             *) exit 6 ;;
         esac
         # Every newly launched Town agent must receive the Founder reporting rule.
